  "AR R.1.4 / TN R.1.4": "No grade 5 AR or TN standard names figurative language in poems; the stanza/structure standard is the closest (same choice as grade 4).",
  "MO": "Grade 5 MO sub-letters differ from grade 4 (point of view is 5.R.2.A.c), so each code was matched on its own text.",
  "TN R.1.1": "No grade 5 TN standard names conflict and plot together; 5.RL.CS.5 (how chapters fit together into a structure) is the closest to how the conflict builds across chapters.",
  "R.3.1": "Figurative language contributing to meaning: TX 10(D) imagery and figurative language for a purpose; AR 5.V.6 and AL 12a interpret figurative language in context; MO 5.R.2.C.c impact of imagery and figurative language; TN 5.RL.CS.4 figurative language in literary text.",
  "R.2.4 / R.3.3": "R.2.4 (track an argument: claim, evidence, reasoning): TX 9(E) argumentative text, AR 5.RC.14.RI, AL 26d and TN 5.RI.IKI.8 reasons and evidence supporting points, MO 5.R.3.B.d and .f. R.3.3 (compare primary and secondary sources): TX 13(D) names primary and secondary sources; AR 5.RC.18.RI, MO 5.R.3.B.b and TN 5.RI.CS.6 compare multiple accounts of the same event; AL has no multiple-accounts standard, so 26c (apply information from multiple sources) is the closest."
